# Draft generated through graph add --draft, then completed by the qpack author.
id:                     E3470
trigger_tool: python
phase: testing
error_signature: qpack latin1 dispatch: UnicodeDecodeError
severity:               3
category: compat, portability
match_keywords: qpack, latin1, PyUnicode_CompareWithASCIIString
title: CPython three-way comparison used as an equality predicate makes alias dispatch unreachable
root_cause: The Python3 compatibility macro returns -1/0/1 while its OR-combined callers expect equality booleans; at least one UTF8 alias comparison is unequal, so UTF8 is always selected and Latin1 is unreachable.
affected_scope: Python3 C extension compatibility macros with equality-predicate callers. qpack0.0.21 is the fixed source example; this is not arbitrary-codec or integer parity.
verification_cmd: python3 -c "import importlib.machinery as m,qpack,qpack._qpack as c; assert isinstance(c.__loader__,m.ExtensionFileLoader); assert qpack.unpackb is c._unpackb; assert qpack.unpackb(bytes.fromhex('81ff'),decode='latin1') == chr(255); print('qpack latin1 native dispatch: PASS')"
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: explicit-equality-predicate
rec_description: Compare the CPython API result explicitly to zero, retain the native extension, and test non-ASCII alias dispatch against independently decoded expected values.
rec_command: Normalize PY_COMPAT_COMPARE to (PyUnicode_CompareWithASCIIString(obj, str) == 0), then rebuild the actual native package and run its unchanged suite plus the narrow alias consumer.
rec_auto_fix: false
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: explicit-backend-diagnostic
fallback_description: Compare raw byte decoding through the real C public API and the existing pure-Python backend to diagnose branch selection; do not disable the C backend to claim success.
fallback_auto_fix: false
forbid_1_pattern: fallback-only success
forbid_1_reason: It bypasses the affected C predicate and does not repair or test the native package.
forbid_1_consequence: The Latin1 dispatch defect remains unverified.
forbid_2_pattern: full C/fallback parity
forbid_2_reason: The scope must remain the supported aliases, bytes and ignore-errors; other integer/codecs have separate contracts.
forbid_2_consequence: Unrelated behavior would be asserted without evidence.
doc_file: knowledge/drafts/E545-draft-QP97.md
rec_impl:               manual
last_updated:               2026-10-19
authors:               QP97
